From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <spolack+claude@mailbox.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:32:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pex: report dropped global messages and failed sends

global_pex_recv() silently discarded anything that was not a PEX message,
had an unknown version or belonged to no dynamic network, and __pex_msg_send()
silently returned the sendto() error. Debugging a host that never gets its
network data then means guessing whether the request left, arrived, or was
rejected. Log each case: the drops in debug mode, the send failure via
perror() like the other socket errors in this file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PVGaNeNhqp11rTLwZ9rM4J
---
 pex-msg.c |  3 +++
 pex.c     | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pex-msg.c b/pex-msg.c
index 79aceb1..7885952 100644
--- a/pex-msg.c
+++ b/pex-msg.c
@@ -346,6 +346,9 @@ int __pex_msg_send(int fd, const void *addr, void *ip_hdr, size_t ip_hdrlen)
 	}
 	hdr->len = orig_len;
 
+	if (ret < 0)
+		perror("pex: send");
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
diff --git a/pex.c b/pex.c
index 9108bb7..eb82668 100644
--- a/pex.c
+++ b/pex.c
@@ -1056,6 +1056,7 @@ global_pex_recv(void *msg, size_t msg_len, struct sockaddr_in6 *addr)
 			network_stun_rx_packet(net, msg, msg_len);
 	}
 
+	/* not necessarily a PEX message: DHT traffic shares this socket */
 	hdr = pex_rx_accept(msg, msg_len, true);
 	if (!hdr)
 		return;
@@ -1063,13 +1064,26 @@ global_pex_recv(void *msg, size_t msg_len, struct sockaddr_in6 *addr)
 	ehdr = (void *)(hdr + 1);
 	data = (void *)(ehdr + 1);
 
-	if (hdr->version != 0)
+	if (hdr->version != 0) {
+		/* The DHT shares this port, and an announced port attracts
+		 * BitTorrent clients: log the first few only. */
+		static int bad_version;
+
+		if (bad_version < 5 && ++bad_version)
+			D("PEX global rx: dropped version %d message (first %d logged)", hdr->version, 5);
 		return;
+	}
 
 	if (hdr->opcode != PEX_MSG_ENROLL) {
 		net = global_pex_find_network(ehdr->auth_id);
-		if (!net || net->config.type != NETWORK_TYPE_DYNAMIC)
+		if (!net || net->config.type != NETWORK_TYPE_DYNAMIC) {
+			static int bad_net;
+
+			if (bad_net < 5 && ++bad_net)
+				D("PEX global rx: op=%d for %s network (first %d logged)", hdr->opcode,
+				  net ? "a non-dynamic" : "an unknown", 5);
 			return;
+		}
 
 		*(uint64_t *)hdr->id ^= pex_network_hash(net->config.auth_key, ehdr->nonce);
 
